  "item": [
    {
      "id": "036a7f12-f9b9-4945-893f-74534a459edd",
      "name": "ReportExport",
      "description": {
        "content": "Asynchronously export reports through impact.com's Jobs system. Recommended for all report downloads.",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "57bc5e85-eb2b-4258-a1eb-65ff8d95732b",
          "name": "Export a report",
          "request": {
            "name": "Export a report",
            "description": {
              "content": "Schedules a report to be exported asynchronously through impact.com's Jobs system. Returns immediately with the initial job status and three URIs to interact with the job.\n\nUse the returned `QueuedUri` to poll job status, `ResultUri` to download the result file once the job has completed, and `ReplayUri` to re-run the same job.\n\n## Available query parameters\n\n- `ResultFormat` — output file format (universal).\n- Report-specific filters — every report accepts its own set of filter parameters (`START_DATE`, `END_DATE`, `SUBAID`, `Advertiser`, etc.). Call `GET /Reports/{ReportId}/MetaData` first to discover which filters a given report supports.\n\n## Error handling\n\nInvalid input is returned as **HTTP 200** with an error envelope in the body — for example, an unknown `ReportId` returns `{\"Status\":\"ERROR\",\"Message\":\"Not permitted to run report ...\"}`. Always check the `Status` field before treating the response as a queued job.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "Agencies",
                ":AccountSID",
                "ReportExport",
                ":ReportId"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "ResultFormat",
                  "value": "CSV",
                  "description": "The file format the exported report should be returned in."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "START_DATE",
                  "value": "<date>",
                  "description": "The start date (inclusive) for the report data, in `YYYY-MM-DD` format. Required by most reports — check the report's `MetaData` to confirm."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "END_DATE",
                  "value": "<date>",
                  "description": "The end date (inclusive) for the report data, in `YYYY-MM-DD` format. Required by most reports — check the report's `MetaData` to confirm."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "SUBAID",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "A program (campaign) ID to refine the report to data from a single program. Required for some reports."
                }
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "key": "AccountSID",
                  "description": "(Required) Your Agency Account SID."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "key": "ReportId",
                  "description": "(Required) The unique ID of the report to export. Use `GET /Reports` to list all reports and find each report's `Id`."
                }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": null
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "id": "f45637bf-1508-4c8c-b220-3c1b7d0e736f",
              "name": "**Success** — the export job was queued. Response includes URIs for polling and downloading the result.\n\n**Error** — invalid input (e.g., bad `ReportId`, unrecognised `ResultFormat`, invalid date) returns the same HTTP 200 status with an error envelope. See the `ErrorResponse` schema and the operation description.",
              "originalRequest": {
                "url": {
                  "path": [
                    "Agencies",
                    ":AccountSID",
                    "ReportExport",
